--- Addendum: step 4 corrected to the concurrent version ---
The sequential second-order attempt in the transcript was correctly rejected
("already used") — consumption happens at checkout, so a lone replay fails.
The real flaw is the check-then-act race, reproduced 2026-10-09 on
127.0.0.1:18094 (separate run, same demo):
  session A: add shirt, apply SAVE10 -> discount=10.00 (no checkout yet)
  session B: add shirt, apply SAVE10 -> discount=10.00 (flag still unused)
  A checkout -> receipt total=15.00 ; B checkout -> receipt total=15.00
ORDERLOG confirms both orders at 15.00 with coupon=SAVE10. The lesson text
(step 4) describes this interleaved version. The fixed build consumes the
coupon atomically at apply time, so the second apply is rejected.
Server on 18094 stopped afterwards; no logic-demo processes remain.
